            "title": "Honda's profit slips as President Trump's tariffs take their toll on Japanese automakers",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Honda reported Friday that its profit for the first fiscal half through September fell 37% from the previous year, as the damage from President Donald Trump\u2019s tariffs offset the lift from solid motorcycle sales.  Tokyo-based Honda Motor Co. recorded a 311.8 billion yen ($2 billion) profit for April-September, down from 494.6 billion yen a year before.  Honda lowered its profit projection for the fiscal year through March 2026 to 300 billion yen ($2 billion), which would be a decline of 64% from 835.8 billion yen the year before.",
